{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And now, let the strength of HaShem be magnified, etc.</b> That You suppress Your anger, as the Sages said: Who is mighty? One who conquers his inclination, as it is said: ״טוב ארך אפים מגבור״." "<b>As You spoke, saying.</b> When I said before You: הודיעני נא את דרכיך — in what measure do You judge Your creatures, and You passed over before me and called: ה' ה' ארך אפים — therefore here too He did not mention ה' ה', for there, ר״ל, it means the attribute of mercy and the attribute of judgment, whereas here He needed to mention only the attribute of mercy. And also El He did not mention here, for it conveys the sense of judge, from the language of ״ואת אילי הארץ לקח״, and also ״וגם אלהים לא תקלל״, which is translated: דיינא לא תלוט. And also רחום וחנון is not written here, because the term רחום applies only together with חנון, and חנינה means giving, as it is said: ״וצדיק חונן ונותן״, and here he was asking only to forgive without giving. But ה', which is the attribute of mercy, and ארך אפים — that He lengthens His anger toward His creatures and does not destroy them immediately — and רב חסד — that He keeps His kindness with His creatures and does not pay them their due — these fit well here. And אמת He did not mention here, for on the contrary, He would not want to fulfill what He said: ״אכנו בדבר ואורישנו״. And נוצר as well does not apply, for perhaps they did not do kindness but rather rebelled." "<b>Bearing iniquity and transgression.</b> But וחטאה He did not mention here, because חטא is only inadvertent, as it is written: ״וחטאה בשגגה״, whereas these were rebels, as it is said: ״אך בה' אל תמרדו״."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:30.766522339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}